Seed Gortex skills when Claude Code is absent

Gortex writes its skill set for exactly one adapter, Claude Code, under
~/.claude/skills. That directory is the only source Sync-AgentSkills can
mirror from, so on a machine without Claude Code the chain broke silently:
auto-detection dropped claude-code from the selection, gortex install never
ran for it, the mirror threw "Skill source not found", and Copilot CLI and
Codex ended up with no gortex-* skills while the installer still reported
success.

The installer now runs the claude-code adapter itself when the skill source
is missing, with hooks and CLAUDE.md suppressed since no Claude session will
consume them. The adapter writes all 21 skills whether or not the Claude CLI
exists, which is what makes this work. Verified against a sandbox config root
holding only .copilot and .codex: 21 skills mirrored, exit 0, and a second
run re-seeds nothing.

Also documents installing Gortex itself. The prerequisites only checked for
the binary and never said how to obtain it, which left a fresh machine stuck
before step one.

